  "description": "PUVYUC crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group C m c a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C128 H104 Dy6 N10 O52 Zn6. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 10 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 10 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 5 O neighbors; Zn3 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 10 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 10 O neighbors; Zn4 (Zn) has 5 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 10 O neighbors; Zn5 (Zn) has 5 O neighbors; Zn6 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 10 O neighbors; Zn7 (Zn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.364-3.873 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.10-108.34°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C128H104Dy6N10O52Zn6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 10 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
